    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present to the market 14 Rossmore Drive. A superb family home in this well established, highly sought after Templeogue location where properties rarely come to market. Nestled in a quiet cul-de-sac, the home enjoys great privacy and a beautiful west-facing rear garden. \r\n\r\nThe light filled accommodation briefly comprises of entrance porch, entrance hallway with guest w.c off. To the left of the hallway is the living room with double doors leading to the dining room and sunroom beyond. There is a spacious kitchen with a wide range of units, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher, sink unit and door to covered side passage providing access to the front and rear gardens. Additionally there is a playroom to the front of the property. \r\n\r\nUpstairs are 4 well proportioned bedrooms, bedroom 1 is to the front with ample built in wardrobes, bedroom 2 is also to the front and bedrooms 3 and 4 are positioned to the rear. The family bathroom completes the internal accommodation with walk in shower, electric shower, w.c and whb. \r\n\r\nOutside to the front is off street parking and lawn and side access. To the rear is a wonderful west facing garden laid out in lawn with paved patio area bordered by mature trees and greenhouse. \r\n\r\nRossmore is a very popular residential area positioned in the heart of Templeogue within walking distance of the village itself, Tymon Park and a range of local primary and secondary schools including Bishop Shannon and Bishop Galvin on your doorstep. \r\n\r\nThe location is second to none and within a 2 minutes walk are a host of local shops at Orwell Shopping Centre including a Supervalu, Orwell News and Farmhouse foods to name a few and Eala and DeJa Brew coffee shops. There are an abundance of local amenities that lie within walking distance at Templeogue village offering popular restaurants, eateries and bars. Many recreational facilities are within the immediate area inc. St Judes and Faughs GAA Club, St Marys Rugby Club and Templeogue Tennis Club. The area is served by excellent public transport providing seamless access to the city centre and offers quick and easy access to the M50."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch \r\nTiled floor and door to property\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall \r\nSolid wood food \r\n\r\nGuest w.c, \r\nW.c, whb \r\n\r\nLiving \r\nCeiling coving, electric fire insert with stone surround and double doors leading to \r\n\r\nDining \r\nCeiling coving and sliding door leading to \r\n\r\nSun room \r\nTiled floor, fully glazed and double doors to garden. \r\n\r\nKitchen \r\nExtensive range of solid wood kitchen units, ceiling coving, plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher, extractor fan, 1 1/3 sink unit, tiled backsplash and door to side. \r\n\r\nCovered side passage \r\nDoor to front and rear garden, boiler off. \r\n\r\nUtility \r\nPlumbed for washing machine and dryer, door leading to front and door leading to living room. \r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nLanding \r\nDado rail and access to attic. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (Front) \r\nWall to wall fitted wardrobes. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (Front) \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (Rear) \r\n\r\nBedroom 4 (Rear) \r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nWalk in shower with electric shower, w.c, whb, tiled floor and walls. \r\n\r\nOutside \r\nOff street parking to the front, lawn and side access. West facing garden to rear with lawn, paved patio area, mature hedging and greenhouse."
      },
      {
